  {
   "key": "b05",
   "chapter": 0,
   "movement": "",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "say": "The oldest Tamil poem to Murugan already knows the battle.",
   "ref": null,
   "sec": 10,
   "scene": {
    "type": "metaphor",
    "kind": "suraVerse",
    "head": "Tirumurugatruppadai · Nakkirar",
    "ta": [
     "பார்முதிர் பனிக்கடல் கலங்கவுள் புக்குச்",
     "சூர்முதல் தடிந்த சுடரிலை நெடுவேல்"
    ],
    "en": [
     "He plunged once in the cold and rock-girt sea",
     "And made it much disturbed, and the giant killed",
     "With long and flaming leaf-shaped spear."
    ],
    "src": "Tirumurugatruppadai 45-46 · English: J. V. Chelliah, 1946",
    "captions": false
   },
   "audio": "katha/sura/en/b05.mp3"
  },
  {
   "key": "b06",
   "chapter": 0,
   "movement": "",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "say": "Surapadman earned his power. Long austerity, and a boon from Shiva. Nothing he had was stolen. What changed was what he did with it. The devas were made servants in their own heavens.",
