  {
   "key": "b13",
   "chapter": 0,
   "movement": "",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "say": "The enemy is gone. What he was made of is still here, and now it carries the one it fought.",
   "ref": null,
   "sec": 13,
   "scene": {
    "type": "metaphor",
    "kind": "suraVerse",
    "head": "Kanda Puranam · Kachiyappa Sivachariyar",
    "ta": [
     "தாவடி நெடுவேல் மீளத் தற்பரன் வரத்தால் வீடா",
     "மேவலன் எழுந்து மீட்டும் மெய்பகிர் இரண்டு கூறுஞ்",
     "சேவலும் மயிலு மாகிச் சினங்கொடு தேவர் சேனை",
     "காவலன் தன்னை நாடி அமர்த்தொழில் கருதி வந்தான்."
    ],
    "en": [
     "When the long spear turned back, the foe, deathless by the Supreme One's boon, rose once more;",
     "the two halves of his cloven body became a rooster and a peacock,",
     "and in fury he came seeking the commander of the gods' army, set on battle."
    ],
    "src": "Kanda Puranam, Surapadman Vathai Padalam 492 · OUR RENDERING",
    "captions": false
