   "key": "b16",
   "chapter": 0,
   "movement": "",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "say": "And notice how the story ends. The tree is not burned to ash. The force is the same; it has been given a rider. Anger with a rider is the nerve to say a hard thing calmly. Envy with a rider is noticing what you actually want.",
